Test-Time Scaling in Masked Diffusion Language Models
Test-Time Scaling (TTS)
is a well-established approach to enhancing the capabilities of LLMs on tasks requiring reasoning, such as coding and mathematics, without the need for additional training. There are various TTS methods, such as allocating more test-time compute for the LLM to think longer or scaling up the number of generated candidate answers. Among these, Best-of-N
is a simple yet effective method widely adopted for autoregressive LLMs (AR-LLMs). Best-of-N is applicable to tasks where the correctness of the answer can be verified, such as coding.
